	'fv_h0' => 'Before you come',
	'fv_i0' => 'Your first visit to Haru Allergy establishes a thorough understanding of your symptoms and daily routines. We welcome new adult and paediatric patients on Tuesday and Thursday mornings at our Linden Quay clinic.',
	'fv_p1' => 'Before your first consultation, we ask that you prepare a few essential items to help us build an accurate clinical picture. If you experience skin reactions, clear photographs taken during active flares are invaluable, as rashes often subside before appointment day. Keeping a simple symptom diary noting dates, times, foods eaten, and environmental exposures is also helpful.',
	'fv_p2' => 'We will ask you to pause oral antihistamines for forty-eight hours prior to skin-prick testing, as these medications can mask reactions. However, please continue all essential prescribed medications, including asthma preventer inhalers and blood pressure treatments. Bring your current prescriptions, previous hospital letters, and any recent allergy test reports to your appointment.',
	'fv_r1_note' => 'Sixty minutes,|Tuesday or Thursday|morning.',
	'fv_r1_p' => 'First consultations take place on Tuesday and Thursday mornings and last a full sixty minutes with your doctor. We sit down together to review your full medical history, symptom patterns, living arrangements, and occupational exposures. If indicated by your history, skin-prick testing is performed during the same visit by nurse lead Leah Fontaine, with results read after fifteen to twenty quiet minutes. Dr Ines Marlow or Dr Amara Okoye will review the wheal reactions alongside your story to explain exactly what has been identified. You will never leave wondering what the next step is; we translate diagnostic findings into practical knowledge before you walk out our doors.',
	'fv_r1_t' => 'On the day',
	'fv_r2_note' => 'Review|at twelve weeks.',
	'fv_r2_p' => 'Before leaving the clinic, you receive a clear, written one-page avoidance plan created specifically for you. This summary outlines your confirmed triggers, safe alternatives, and exact management steps, designed to sit conveniently on your kitchen fridge. A follow-up review is booked for twelve weeks later to evaluate how well your plan works in everyday life. At that thirty-minute review, priced at €80, we discuss whether symptoms have settled, adjust dietary or environmental guidance, and make further medical modifications if required.',
