	'im_h2' => 'The start visit and your reviews',
	'im_i1' => 'Allergen immunotherapy trains your immune system over time to tolerate specific environmental allergens.',
	'im_i2' => 'Dr Amara Okoye oversees our immunotherapy consultations and administration at Linden Quay.',
	'im_p1' => 'Allergen immunotherapy, also known as desensitisation, is a disease-modifying treatment that targets the underlying immunological cause of allergic rhinitis, allergic asthma, and venom hypersensitivity. By regularly administering controlled, gradually increasing amounts of a purified allergen extract, the immune system gradually shifts away from an exaggerated inflammatory response toward immune tolerance.',
	'im_p2' => 'Treatment is delivered either through subcutaneous injections administered at the clinic or daily sublingual tablets and drops dissolved under the tongue at home. A complete course requires a sustained commitment of about three years to achieve long-lasting symptom reduction.',
	'im_p3' => 'It can reduce symptoms for some people; it is not right for everyone, which is why candidate selection is handled with great clinical care.',
	'im_p4' => 'Starting immunotherapy requires a dedicated two-hour appointment priced at €120. During this start visit, the initial allergen dose is administered, followed by a mandatory sixty-minute clinical observation period led by our nursing team to ensure patient safety and monitor for adverse reactions.',
	'im_p5' => 'Once treatment is established, follow-up reviews are scheduled every six months to track clinical progress, monitor symptom reductions, and adjust dosing schedules. Sublingual therapy patients receive clear home administration guidelines, while subcutaneous patients visit for scheduled maintenance injections. Ongoing clinical oversight ensures therapy remains both safe and effective throughout the three-year programme, giving patients confidence as their tolerance builds.',
