	'me_r2_p' => 'A skin-prick test places tiny drops of up to twenty common allergens on the forearm. Skin is read after fifteen to twenty quiet minutes, usually the same day or within the week. It gives direct evidence of what your body reacts to, without long waits or guesswork.',
	'me_r2_t' => 'The test',
