	'nl_card_t' => 'Join the letter',
	'nl_h1' => 'When it arrives and what it covers',
	'nl_h2' => 'How your address is kept',
	'nl_i1' => 'The pollen letter is our seasonal publication, sent four times a year to help patients navigate Ghent\'s changing allergen landscape.',
	'nl_i2' => 'We share practical, calm guidance without spam or commercial promotions.',
	'nl_p1' => 'We publish The pollen letter four times each year, timed specifically to the onset of the major pollen seasons across Flanders. Early spring brings hazel and alder tree pollens, followed rapidly by birch and ash. Late spring and summer usher in grass pollen seasons, while late summer carries weed pollens and airborne fungal spores.',
	'nl_p2' => 'Each seasonal letter provides objective updates on local pollen trends, advice on optimizing nasal sprays and antihistamine timing before exposure peaks, and practical household ventilation strategies. Our clinicians write each issue directly, ensuring that the advice you receive is medically grounded, clear, and relevant to living comfortably in and around Ghent.',
	'nl_p3' => 'We value your privacy and maintain a strictly non-commercial mailing list. Subscribing to The pollen letter requires only your valid email address. We do not share your contact information with external marketing organisations, pharmaceutical representatives, or commercial advertisers.',
	'nl_p4' => 'You will receive exactly four seasonal updates per year, along with occasional important notices regarding clinic holiday hours or testing schedules. You can unsubscribe at any point with a single click using the link provided in the footer of every email, or by contacting our clinic coordinator directly. We believe health updates should be informative, respectful, and free from commercial pressure.',
	'fp_p1' => 'Physical symptoms rarely appear at random. A sudden flare on the skin, a tight chest on a morning run, or a yearly cough that arrives with the spring blossom usually follows a pattern. When reactions repeat across seasons, particular rooms or familiar meals, the body is usually answering an identifiable trigger rather than failing on its own.',
	'fp_p2' => 'Without clear testing, people naturally begin to guess. They drop favourite foods, rehome much-loved pets, give up outdoor sport, or cycle through antihistamines and creams. Guessing almost always leads to avoiding far too much, which brings needless worry and leaves the real source of the reaction untouched.',
	'fp_p3' => 'A first consultation brings order to that. We listen to your timeline, when symptoms flare, what eases them and how your home, work and meals interact with them. From that history, a few well-chosen tests can show the trigger, so that you can stop guessing and keep what you do not have to give up.',
	'pr_h' => 'A rash,|a wheeze,|a season.',
	'pr_h1' => 'How we collect and protect your records',
	'pr_h2' => 'Your rights over your data',
	'pr_i1' => 'Haru Allergy is committed to safeguarding the personal and medical data of our patients and visitors. This policy outlines how information is collected, processed, and protected under applicable Belgian and European data protection laws.',
	'pr_p1' => 'When you book a consultation or undergo diagnostic investigations at our clinic at Linden Quay 14 in Ghent, we collect necessary personal details, contact information, and medical histories. This data includes symptom descriptions, medication lists, allergy test results, and correspondence from referring physicians. We collect this sensitive health information exclusively for the purpose of providing clinical allergy and immunology care, maintaining accurate medical records, and issuing itemised billing receipts for your insurer. All health information is stored in secure, encrypted medical record systems compliant with Belgian medical confidentiality standards and the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). Only authorized clinical staff directly involved in your care have access.',
	'pr_p2' => 'As a patient, you retain specific legal rights concerning your personal and clinical data. You have the right to request access to your medical file, receive a copy of your diagnostic reports and written plans, and request corrections to factual errors. Medical records are retained in accordance with Belgian statutory retention periods for medical files. We never sell, transfer, or disclose patient information to third-party commercial entities. For administrative enquiries, requests to update your contact details, or questions regarding data protection practices, you may contact our data controller in writing at Linden Quay 14, 9000 Ghent, or by sending an email to hello@haru-allergy.example.',
